A||||8||Mark||OEM Dogbone for V6||||1||
Z||000000||Mark||11-21-2000||07:53 PM||||Does anyone have a part number for an OEM-style V6 dogbone (Anchor, Balkamp, Moog, etc.)? I know FS sells them, but I prefer to buy from a local parts store.  <P>I've searched on the subject and found people claiming they were able to buy a dogbone from NAPA.  I haven't been so lucky...they just say "not available".<P>I ordered one from Carparts.com.  What I received was a 4-cyl 'bone (about 6 7/8" center-to-center).  It turns out that both Carparts.com and Wrenchead.com list the same part number (Anchor #2761) for both 4 cyl and V6 engines!  Go figure.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-22-2000||01:56 AM||||we sell the OEM struts for the V-6 -- call us at the Fiero Shop - 1-510-233-4376.......<P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
