Z||000005||theogre||11-22-2000||01:28 PM||||look it up as a torque reaction strut or shock. They should be available but you'll likely have to order it thru most stores. Pep Boys got the last one for me in about a week. (Mine is a 4 cyl but the same company makes the 6 cyl one.) The 4 cyl one was nearly $40us.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||11-22-2000||04:19 PM||||$42!!!!!!!!!! hokey smokes! Yeah, go aftermarket. <P>Wow, I know dealers mark stuff up, but they must have to pay for a crystal cathedral there. I just bought one here for $18 from the Chevy dealer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mark||11-22-2000||04:34 PM||||True, this is a really nice looking dealership - I guess the parts department sure helps to pay the bills!  <P>The best price I could find, about $33 with shipping (and a 33% discount coupon), was from Carparts.com.  Unfortunately, they (and Wrenchead.com) have an application error in their website.  That's why I was interested in part numbers. I guess I'll try the local Chevy dealer...||||reg||1
